      "writtenOn": "2017-03-09T04:57:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had added this here so that typec_set_input_current_limit() wouldn\u0027t get called here when the CHG port was connected to a charger that supported PD messaging. I didn\u0027t want the VBUS on indication to be available until the PS_RDY message is received. However, thinking about it more, this special consideration is not really necessary, since that can be handled in the port manager code that looks at the VBUS state from the CHG port. So I removed this block and added the CONFIG_USB_PD_DTS to the places that are setting typec_curr which allows the block below to be used as is.",
      "parentUuid": "24cf1e3e_43398215",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2572,
        "startChar": 0,
